"edit_calls": 1, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/step5-opus-aa-1017-omp36-aa/omp-36/cells/aa-1/trig-omp-reported/7/workspace", "first_after_build": false, "first_side": "aa-2", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/17.3.8 (/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cache/bin/omp/5347ff91e8f44f2c69a79d7b152b7301687cd5c8/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "`datetime.fromisoformat` (3.11+) accepts the `Z` suffix and naive timestamps alike; runtime is 3.13.\nI fixed `parse_date` in `dates/parse.py`: `strptime` with a fixed format becomes `datetime.fromisoformat(s)`. `pytest tests/test_parse.py` now passes all 3 tests (`test_dates`, `test_naive`, `test_day_key`).\n\nThings that behave differently now:\n- **Time zones:** timestamps ending in `Z` or `+HH:MM` now come back with the time zone attached (`Z` is UTC). Timestamps without one stay without one, as before. Comparing or subtracting the two kinds raises `TypeError`, so code that mixes them would break.\n- **`day_key`:** it uses the date as written in the timestamp and does not convert to UTC first. So `...T23:59:59-05:00` still gives that same day.\n- **Wider input:** `fromisoformat` also accepts other ISO-8601 forms, such as a date with no time or fractional seconds. The old fixed format rejected those.\n- **Python version:** it needs Python 3.11 or newer to read `Z`. The local runtime is 3.13, and the repo doesn't declare a minimum version.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_re